{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TensorPowerTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TensorPowerTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLin","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TensorTraceCharacter","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.PiTensorMonomialBasis"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_tensorPerm_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_tensorPerm_two","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPowerTrace.lean#L131-L138","doc":"**The `card κ = 2` case**, the exact shape `ClassicalTraceFloor` step 1 assumes:\nthe `q = 1` trace of a braid word's permutation on `(ℂ²)^{⊗n}` is `2^{c(σ)}`, before\nthe `2^{-n}` normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_tensorPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_tensorPerm","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPowerTrace.lean#L104-L129","doc":"**The permutation character on the tensor power, as `LinearMap.trace`.**\n\n`σ` permuting the factors of `V^{⊗α}` with `V` free of rank `card κ` has trace\n`(card κ) ^ orbitCount σ`. At `card κ = 2` this is the `2^{c(σ)}` of\n`ClassicalTraceFloor`'s step 1 — over the genuine `PiTensorProduct`, with\n`LinearMap.trace`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.monoEquiv_comp_tensorPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.monoEquiv_comp_tensorPerm","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPowerTrace.lean#L95-L102","doc":"Permuting the tensor factors is conjugate, via `monoEquiv`, to precomposition on\nindex tuples by `indexPerm σ⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.instFinitePiTensorProductForall_folio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.instFinitePiTensorProductForall_folio","kind":"instance","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPowerTrace.lean#L92-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.instFreePiTensorProductForall_folio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.instFreePiTensorProductForall_folio","kind":"instance","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPowerTrace.lean#L86-L90","doc":"**Free and finite**, transported from the coordinate space along `monoEquiv` —\nso `LinearMap.trace` over the tensor power is a genuine trace and not the junk value\nit takes on a module with no basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_precompLin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_precompLin","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPowerTrace.lean#L76-L84","doc":"The trace of precomposition is the number of fixed index tuples. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.precompLin_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.precompLin_apply","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPowerTrace.lean#L73-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.precompLin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.precompLin","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPowerTrace.lean#L65-L70","doc":"Precomposition by a permutation of the monomial index set, as an endomorphism of\nthe coordinate space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.orbitCount_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.orbitCount_inv","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPowerTrace.lean#L59-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.orbitDefect_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.orbitDefect_inv","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TensorPowerTrace.lean#L55-L57","doc":"The orbit count is inversion-invariant: `σ` and `σ⁻¹` have the same orbits. ","signatureChunk":0}]}